<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  The heirloom razor. Suggestion 1.5.

  Razors are named, kept for generations and handed down inside a house. Royalty's
  persona weapons are exactly that mechanic: a weapon that bonds to one wielder,
  carries traits, and has a generated name. The project's original plan for the razor
  (Weapons_RimRising.xml) was "the razor becomes a persona weapon"; it was dropped when
  Royalty was not yet a dependency. It is now.

  STRUCTURE. ParentName BaseWeapon_Bladelink, which is Royalty's abstract for persona
  melee weapons - mirrored from Vanilla Factions Expanded - Empire's
  VFEE_MeleeWeapon_ToxbladeBladelink (1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Weapons/MeleeBladelink.xml),
  which inherits the bladelink and generated-name comps from that parent and declares
  nothing of its own but stats, graphic, sounds, classes and tools. This def does the
  same, and the tool numbers are the ordinary razor's.

  THE WHIP (user, 2026-10-10: every razor has it). The comps are restated with
  Inherit="False", as on the ordinary razor, to swap CompEquippable for
  CompEquippableAbility (a subclass - both at once would double the equippable).
  The restated list is BaseWeapon's (Forbiddable, Styleable) plus
  BaseWeapon_Bladelink's (CompQuality, BladelinkWeapon with biocodeOnEquip,
  GeneratedName with NamerWeaponBladelink), read from Core and Royalty.

  NEVER CRAFTED. No recipeMaker. generateCommonality low, tradeability None - it is
  found on a dead Olympic Knight or granted by a quest, never built or bought.
  tradeability values and generateCommonality seen on VFE/VWE weapons.

  RR_RazorBearer + RR_CasteRestricted so the Harmony restriction applies and only
  Gold and Bronzie kinds roll it. A bonded weapon that will not let a Red hold it is
  the setting's own line about razors, for free.

  CE: 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/Weapons_RimRising.xml patches its tools, as
  the validator requires (CEToolsUnpatched).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BaseWeapon_Bladelink">
    <defName>RR_Weapon_Razor_Heirloom</defName>
    <label>heirloom razor</label>
    <description>A razor that has been carried before. The hilt is worn to the shape of several hands, and the blade has a name that was given to it in another century by someone who is now a portrait.\n\nIt will bond to one bearer and refuse every other. The house it came from would say that is the blade recognising blood. The Orange who serviced it would say it is a lock.</description>
    <techLevel>Ultra</techLevel>
    <equippedAngleOffset>-65</equippedAngleOffset>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Equipment/WeaponMelee/RR_RazorHeirloom</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Interact_BladelinkMonoSword</soundInteract>
    <meleeHitSound>MeleeHit_BladelinkMonoSword</meleeHitSound>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>4200</MarketValue>
      <Mass>1.4</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <generateCommonality>0.3</generateCommonality>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <smeltable>false</smeltable>
    <burnableByRecipe>false</burnableByRecipe>
    <weaponTags>
      <li>RR_RazorBearer</li>
      <li>RR_CasteRestricted</li>
    </weaponTags>
    <weaponClasses>
      <li>Melee</li>
      <li>MeleePiercer</li>
    </weaponClasses>
    <comps Inherit="False">
      <li Class="CompProperties_EquippableAbility">
        <abilityDef>RR_RazorWhip</abilityDef>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Forbiddable"/>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Styleable"/>
      <li>
        <compClass>CompQuality</compClass>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_BladelinkWeapon">
        <biocodeOnEquip>true</biocodeOnEquip>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_GeneratedName">
        <nameMaker>NamerWeaponBladelink</nameMaker>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>hilt</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>10</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.5</cooldownTime>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>point</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Stab</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>26</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.9</cooldownTime>
        <armorPenetration>0.95</armorPenetration>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>edge</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Cut</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>27</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.9</cooldownTime>
        <armorPenetration>0.95</armorPenetration>
      </li>
    </tools>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
